  "walkthrough-note": "THE FIRST-CONTACT WALKTHROUGH'S MAP SITES (spoke W, ideas/plans/onboarding-walkthrough.md). Ids only, never prose and never coordinates, for the reason the reveal's beats carry ids only: a sidecar that spelled a label out would ship the previous wording the day a content pass renames it. \`unfold\` is the box the TOOL opens on beat 4 and \`edit\` is the STATEMENT the reader drags on beat 5, with the effect read at \`read\`; the climax site was signed off 2026-08-07 (a single statement edit, never an evidence and never multi-handle). \`through\` and \`steady\` are optional colour: the intermediate step the consequence travels through, and a node that visibly holds still. Re-measured 2026-08-07 at asi-soon=0.1: everyone-dies 0.759 -> 0.581, if-built 0.883 -> 0.664, asi-soon itself implies 0.348, shutdown 0.970 -> 0.971 (both render 97%, so the steady line says 'holds at 97%', never 'does not move'). Re-measured 2026-09-08 under the G network reference (D161, the default since that day; the reader's number replaces the author's pair on the root and enters as a point at the cap): everyone-dies 0.827 -> 0.523, if-built 0.910 -> 0.555, asi-soon itself implies 0.124 against the reader's 0.1 (a residual of 0.024, past the tint's 0.01 tolerance, so the reader's own bar colours and the pushback sentence says the map refused the number by that much), shutdown 0.994 -> 0.994 at three decimals (both render 99%). The kernel pins are in mvp/packages/editor/tests/walkthrough.test.ts; the python solve (solve_map.py --override asi-soon=0.1) agrees to three decimals. A beat whose ids this map no longer has is SKIPPED, not fatal (tours/walkthrough.ts beatIsReachable).",
